<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<addon id="plugin.video.iptvbalkan"
       name="IPTV Balkan"
       version="1.41.0"
       provider-name="IPTV Balkan">
  <requires>
    <import addon="xbmc.python" version="3.0.0"/>
    <!-- pycryptodome was declared here for EON's AES-CBC stream signature, and REMOVED after the first
         real box: Kodi reported it installed while the module was a stub with no `lib` directory, so
         `import Crypto` failed and no channel would play — and Kodi will not install the real one over
         a dependency it already considers satisfied. The cipher now lives in resources/lib/aes.py,
         verified against the NIST vectors. One less thing that is somebody else's decision per box. -->
    <import addon="inputstream.adaptive" version="20.0.0"/>
    <!-- The PVR half. This addon does not implement the PVR API (that would mean C++ and a separate
         build per architecture); it writes M3U + XMLTV and lets IPTV Simple present them, which is what
         gives us the native channel list, EPG grid, groups and catch-up on every platform from one zip. -->
    <!-- NOT optional any more. Kodi installs (and enables) a required dependency by itself when the
         addon is installed, which is the whole "it should just work on one click" — an optional one it
         quietly ignores, leaving a user with a working addon, no channel list, and nothing saying why.
         pvr.iptvsimple is in the official Kodi repository for every platform, so it always resolves;
         the risk of a required dependency (the install fails if it cannot be found) does not apply. -->
    <import addon="pvr.iptvsimple" version="20.0.0"/>
    <!-- REQUIRED for the same reason pvr.iptvsimple is, and it was missing until it was noticed on a
         box that only worked by luck. EON channels carry `#KODIPROP:inputstream=inputstream.ffmpegdirect`
         (it is the only engine here that can re-request a catch-up URL with a new {utc}, which is what
         makes archive seeking exist at all). Without it installed those channels fail to open with no
         message naming the missing piece — the test box happened to have it, so nothing ever said so.
         Declaring it means Kodi fetches it from the official repository on install, on every platform. -->
    <import addon="inputstream.ffmpegdirect" version="20.0.0"/>
  </requires>

  <extension point="xbmc.python.pluginsource" library="default.py">
    <provides>video</provides>
  </extension>
  <!-- Background worker: refreshes the catalogue on its own schedule and regenerates the playlist. -->
  <extension point="xbmc.service" library="service.py"/>

  <extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
    <!-- Stalker is deliberately NOT listed: there is no stalker.py. Advertising a provider that does
         not exist is how a customer buys the wrong thing. -->
    <summary lang="en_GB">IPTV Balkan — multi-provider client (EON, Iris, Yettel, Move, Xtream, M3U)</summary>
    <description lang="en_GB">Logs in to your own provider account, builds a channel list and guide, and hands playback to inputstream.adaptive. Every network identity (User-Agent, origin, referer, device descriptors) is configurable, and a full request trace can be exported when a provider changes something.
      Film and series artwork and descriptions come from TMDB. This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.</description>
    <summary lang="sr_RS">IPTV Balkan — klijent za više provajdera (EON, Iris, Yettel, Move, Xtream, M3U)</summary>
    <description lang="sr_RS">Prijavljuje se na tvoj nalog kod provajdera, gradi listu kanala i vodič, a reprodukciju predaje inputstream.adaptive dodatku. Svaki deo mrežnog identiteta (User-Agent, origin, referer, opis uređaja) je podesiv, a pun trag zahteva može da se izveze kada provajder nešto promeni.
      Podaci o filmovima i serijama: TMDB. Ovaj dodatak koristi TMDB i TMDB API, ali TMDB ga nije odobrio niti sertifikovao.</description>
    <platform>all</platform>
    <license>Proprietary</license>
    <!-- The files exist now, so they are declared. Both are generated by tools/makeart.py from the
         Android app's own launcher mark, path for path — two halves of one product should not have two
         logos. Without this block Kodi draws a grey placeholder in the list a customer browses BEFORE
         installing anything, which is the loudest "unfinished" signal a finished addon can send. -->
    <assets>
      <icon>icon.png</icon>
      <fanart>fanart.jpg</fanart>
    </assets>
    <forum>https://t.me/+d7XjefqrYkkyYjlk</forum>
    <!-- Shown by Kodi on the addon's own page, and it is the only release note most people ever read.
         Written for a viewer — what changed on their television — rather than as a commit log. -->
    <news>
1.41.0
- Move: program (EPG) je bio prazan — 301 kanal, nijedna emisija. Servis odbija da posalje
  vise od odredjenog broja sati odjednom, a dodatak je trazio celu nedelju. Sada prvo izmeri
  koliko servis prima pa uzima program u delovima, pocevsi od onoga sto ide sada.
- EON Video klub sada pocinje onako kako izgleda i u zvanicnoj aplikaciji: Filmovi,
  Serije, Deca i Dokumentarni, a u njima operaterove sopstvene police (Najgledanije,
  Novo dodato, Preporuceno). Stari spisak po kanalima je i dalje tu, red nize.
  </news>
  </extension>
</addon>
